<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Saar Territory</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1935 CE · capital Saarbrücken</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Coal-mining region on the French border governed by the League of Nations for 15 years before voting to return to Germany.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> separated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saar-river">Saar</a> basin from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1920 and placed it under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> for 15 years, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> granted ownership of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> mines as reparation for damage to French mines. A plebiscite was to decide its future afterwards.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A five-member Governing Commission appointed by the League ran the territory, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> holding the chair for many years. The French franc became the currency and the area was within the French customs zone. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">Coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> dominated the economy. After 1933 opponents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Hitler</a> sought refuge there and campaigned for keeping the status quo.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the plebiscite of 13 January 1935, about 90.7 per cent voted for reunion with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The territory returned to Germany on 1 March 1935, a propaganda triumph for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazism">Nazis</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/saar-territory.jpg" alt="Saar Territory" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saar_1920-1935.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1935 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Saarbrücken</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Geoffrey Knox</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Germany</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Territory of the Saar Basin, Saargebiet</dd></dl></aside></div>
